# USB audio and MIDI.
#
# The audio interface of the reference machine is a USB class-compliant
# device (document 0, M-12), and so will most others be: the one driver
# serves them all. Built in, like everything the machine needs to do its
# job: no module has to be found and loaded when an interface is plugged
# in. With nothing plugged in the driver does nothing.
#
# MIDI 2.0 (and with it the Universal MIDI Packet layer) is part of the
# same driver. The hardware-dependent interface (SND_HWDEP), raw MIDI and
# PCM are selected by it; they are named here because other parts of
# dawOS rely on them: the control protocol of the interface goes through
# hwdep (ADR 0008).
CONFIG_SND_USB_AUDIO=y
CONFIG_SND_USB_AUDIO_MIDI_V2=y
CONFIG_SND_UMP=y
CONFIG_SND_HWDEP=y
CONFIG_SND_RAWMIDI=y
